line	<str>Run north and east across the bridge and west past the second wooden bridge to talk to Dondakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to western Keldagrim and talk to the Dwarven Engineer in the Trading Consortium's palace smithing shop.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Ice Mountain entrance of the Dwarven Mine and talk to Rolad in the east house (chat will disengage once then re-engage).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go down the trapdoor to the Dwarven Mine. Complete the following in any order until you receive the respective pages:</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rolad. (chat will again disengage then re-engage)</str>
line	
line	<str>Read Dwarven lore in its entirety and keep it for later.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to the Keldagrim mines and talk to Dondakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a gold bar on him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to any furnace and use a gold bar on the furnace to make a golden cannon ball. Edgeville is recommended for easy fairy ring or Keldagrim minecart access.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the golden cannon ball on Dondakan to receive a Schematic.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the Dwarven lore book to receive the base schematics.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to the Dwarf Engineer at the Western Trade Consortium to get the Schematics.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your gold bar on the nearby anvil to make a gold helmet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the pub in the White Wolf Mountain passage and speak to Khorvak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Assemble the schematics per below to get the completed Schematic:</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your Gold helmet and pickaxe and prepare to kill a level 75-125 Arzinian Avatar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dondakan with the schematics.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Mine 6 OR 15 <col=800000>Gold ore</col> (keep them in your inventory. If you aren't going to get 15, just get 6 as there is no benefit before 15). Getting 15 reduces the boss's level from 125 to 75, so this is recommended for lower-level players.</col>
